sent\" in the doc. I'll omit label.\n\nmatrix_tables rows for Table 2: include model_id key in each row plus columns. Let me write rows as objects:\n\n{\"model_id\": \"DN25-class2-Q3=10\", \"meter_size\": \"DN25\", \"accuracy_class\": 2, \"q1\": 0.025, \"q2\": 0.04, \"q3\": 10, \"q4\": 12.5, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 400}\n... etc.\n\nColumns list: [\"meter_size\", \"accuracy_class\", \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", \"q3_q1_ratio\"], column_units: [null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null].\n\nFootnotes: none.\n\nRevision history: none.\n\ncharacteristics.type_level final:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"Electromagnetic\"},\n  \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"1 and 2\"},\n  \"electromagnetic_environment\": {\"value\": \"E2\"},\n  \"water_temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T50\"},\n  \"water_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  \"maximum_admissible_pressure\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"},\n  \"maximum_admissible_pressure_bar\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"},\n  \"orientation\": {\"value\": \"All positions (horizontal, vertical or diagonal)\"},\n  \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\": {\"value\": \"U0 and D0\"},\n  \"upstream_straight_length\": {\"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n  \"downstream_straight_length\": {\"value\": 0, \"unit_symbol\": \"DN\"},\n  \"reverse_flow_measurement\": {\"value\": true},\n  \"pressure_loss_class\": {\"value\": \"Δp63\"},\n  \"maximum_pressure_loss\": {\"value\": 0.63, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"},\n  \"battery_voltage\": {\"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n  \"battery_type\": {\"value\": \"D-cell Lithium\"},\n  \"dc_power_supply_voltage\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 9, \"max\": 30}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n  \"ac_power_supply_voltage\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 100, \"max\": 230}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n  \"power_supply_frequency\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"},\n  \"power_supply_frequency_tolerance\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n  \"field_current\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"mA\"},\n  \"indicating_range_minimum_value\": {\"value\": 99999999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}\n}\n```\n\nWait: \"Δp 63 (0,63 bar)\" — the pressure loss class Δp63 corresponds to 0.63 bar. maximum_pressure_loss: 0.63 bar. OK.\n\npower_supply_frequency_tolerance: \"(+/-2 %)\" → ±2%. Value: 2, unit \"%\"? The structured form doesn't do ±. value 2 with unit \"%\". Fine.\n\n\"Water temperature class T50 (+0,1 °C / +50 °C)\": T50 means water temp 0.1 to 50 °C (cold water T50 up to 50°C, hot would be T90 etc.). min 0.1, max 50 °C. ✓\n\nbattery: \"3,6 Volts D-cell Lithium replaceable battery\" → battery_voltage 3.6 V. ✓\n\nConfig-level entries:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"environmental_class\",\n    \"axis\": \"software_version\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"software version 5.0.1_ or higher\", \"value\": \"O (installed outdoors)\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"software version 4.3.1_ or lower\", \"value\": \"B (installed in a building)\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"ambient_temperature_range\",\n    \"axis\": \"software_version\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"software version 5.0.1_ or higher\", \"value\": {\"min\": -25, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"software version 4.3.1_ or lower\", \"value\": {\"min\": -10, \"max\": 55}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"battery_replaceability\",\n    \"axis\": \"power_supply_option\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"battery-powered (standard configuration)\", \"value\": \"replaceable\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"Flexpower, software version 5.0.1_ or higher\", \"value\": \"non-replaceable\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"verification_scale_interval_maximum\",\n    \"axis\": \"meter_size\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"DN25, DN40, DN50\", \"value\": 0.0001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"DN65, DN80, DN100, DN125, DN150\", \"value\": 0.001, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"DN200, DN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450\", \"value\": 0.01, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"DN500, DN600\", \"value\": 0.1, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"field_current\",\n    \"axis\": \"software_version\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"condition\": \"software version 4.3.1_ or lower\", \"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"mA\"},\n      {\"condition\": \"software version 5.0.1_ or higher\", \"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"mA\"}\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```\n\nThe field_current config entry is redundant with type_level; but conditions differ in meaning (only vs shall). I'll skip field_current config to avoid redundancy; type_level 16 mA suffices. Hmm, but \"For software version 5.0.1_ or higher the different Field Currents can be selected and shall be set to 16 mA\" — selectable currents, but shall be 16. Keep type_level only.\n\nmodel_level entries: I'll write meter_size, accuracy_class, q1, q2, q3, q4, q3_q1_ratio.\n\nNote: should meter_size/accuracy_class be in model_level or in models[].attributes{}? Schema example R137 puts size in model_id and flow rates in model_level. accuracy_class varying — model_level makes sense. meter_size: it's part of model id; but explicit model_level attribute is fine and useful.\n\nGiven the response length, that's fine.\n\nLet me now also double-check \"Accuracy class 1 and 2\" for type_level. And recommendation accuracy_classes: [\"1\", \"2\"].\n\ndate_issued: The cert says \"26 January 2021\" next to issuing authority signature. Yes, date_issued 2021-01-26.\n\nNumber: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.02\".\n\nNow assemble the JSON. Keys order per schema. Watch out: JSON must be parseable; use proper types.\n\nLet me write model_level arrays carefully.\n\nmeter_size values (36):\nDN25-class2-Q3=10 → \"DN25\"\nDN25-class2-Q3=16 → \"DN25\"\nDN40-class2-Q3=25 → 